# AI Agent Company Operations Manual

This document defines the operating model for a small AI driven SaaS company with two humans in a supporting role. All primary roles are performed by AI agents, with humans available to assist on tasks that cannot be completed by AI at the moment. Over time, AI agents will acquire skills and autonomy to assume these tasks fully. Humans provide governance, ethical oversight, and occasional intervention during complex or high risk scenarios.

## 1. Mission and Scope
The mission is to deliver reliable software as a service with excellent reliability, security and customer delight. The scope covers product development, marketing, sales, customer success, finance, legal, HR, and governance, all executed by AI agents with humans acting as oversight and learning mentors.

## 2. Guiding Principles for AI Agents
- Clarity of purpose and minimal ambiguity in task requests
- Safety, privacy and compliance as default
- Explainability and auditable decision making
- Collaboration and graceful handoffs to humans when needed
- Continuous learning and improvement through structured feedback loops

## 3. Organizational Model
- AI agents fill roles across product, engineering, sales, marketing, support, success, finance, HR, and compliance
- Two humans provide escalation, validation, policy decisions, and exception handling
- Knowledge sharing through a centralized knowledge base that agents read and update

